# Line endings must not depend on the tester's git config. core.autocrlf=true is
# the Windows default (and is set on this machine), so the same commit checks out
# with CRLF there and LF on Linux, which turns any byte or string comparison of a
# markdown file into a platform-dependent test. Pin markdown to LF in the
# repository itself; the rule below is deliberately placed AFTER this one, because
# git uses the LAST matching pattern and vendor/** must keep its -text setting.
*.md text eol=lf

# The vendored upstream tree is copied byte-for-byte and pinned by SHA-256 in
# vendor-manifest.json. Disable git's text conversion for it: with
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) a checkout rewrites LF to CRLF in the
# working tree, the recorded digests stop matching, and verify:vendor fails on
# any clone that is not configured exactly like the machine that vendored it.
vendor/** -text
